---An object representing a Base Report
---@class plaid.BaseReport
---@field report_id string
---@field date_generated string The date and time when the Base Report was created, in [ISO 8601](https://wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format (e.g. "2018-04-12T03:32:11Z").
---@field days_requested number The number of days of transaction history requested.
---@field client_report_id? string|distilled.Null Client-generated identifier, which can be used by lenders to track loan applications.
---@field items plaid.BaseReportItemsList Data returned by Plaid about each of the Items included in the Base Report.
---@field attributes? plaid.BaseReportUserAttributes
---@field [string] any

---Base Report information about an account
---@class plaid.BaseReportAccount
---@field account_id string Plaid's unique identifier for the account. This value will not change unless Plaid can't reconcile the account with the data returned by the financial institution. This may occur, for example, when the name of the account changes. If this happens a new `account_id` will be assigned to the account. If an account with a specific `account_id` disappears instead of changing, the account is likely closed. Closed accounts are not returned by the Plaid API. Like all Plaid identifiers, the `account_id` is case sensitive.
---@field balances plaid.BaseReportAccountBalances
---@field consumer_disputes plaid.BaseReportAccountConsumerDisputesList The information about previously submitted valid dispute statements by the consumer
---@field mask string|distilled.Null The last 2-4 alphanumeric characters of an account's official account number. Note that the mask may be non-unique between an Item's accounts, and it may also not match the mask that the bank displays to the user.
---@field metadata plaid.BaseReportAccountMetadata
---@field name string The name of the account, either assigned by the user or by the financial institution itself
---@field official_name string|distilled.Null The official name of the account as given by the financial institution
---@field type plaid.AccountType
---@field subtype plaid.AccountSubtype|distilled.Null
---@field days_available number The duration of transaction history available within this report for this Item, typically defined as the time since the date of the earliest transaction in that account.
---@field transactions plaid.BaseReportAccountTransactionsList Transaction history associated with the account. Transaction history returned by endpoints such as `/transactions/get` or `/investments/transactions/get` will be returned in the top-level `transactions` field instead. Some transactions may have their details masked in accordance with the FCRA. These will appear with a `credit_category` of `MASKED_TRANSACTION_CATEGORY`.
---@field owners plaid.BaseReportAccountOwnersList Data returned by the financial institution about the account owner or owners. For business accounts, the name reported may be either the name of the individual or the name of the business, depending on the institution. Multiple owners on a single account will be represented in the same `owner` object, not in multiple owner objects within the array. This array can also be empty if no owners are found.
---@field holder_category? any
---@field ownership_type plaid.OwnershipType|distilled.Null
---@field historical_balances? plaid.BaseReportAccountHistoricalBalancesList Calculated data about the historical balances on the account. Currently not supported by `brokerage` or `investment` accounts.
---@field account_insights? plaid.BaseReportAccountInsights
---@field attributes? plaid.BaseReportAttributes
---@field [string] any

---Information about an account's balances.
---@class plaid.BaseReportAccountBalances
---@field available number|distilled.Null The amount of funds available to be withdrawn from the account, as determined by the financial institution. For `credit`-type accounts, the `available` balance typically equals the `limit` less the `current` balance, less any pending outflows plus any pending inflows. For `depository`-type accounts, the `available` balance typically equals the `current` balance less any pending outflows plus any pending inflows. For `depository`-type accounts, the `available` balance does not include the overdraft limit. For `investment`-type accounts (or `brokerage`-type accounts for API versions 2018-05-22 and earlier), the `available` balance is the total cash available to withdraw as presented by the institution. Note that not all institutions calculate the `available` balance. In the event that `available` balance is unavailable, Plaid will return an `available` balance value of `null`. Available balance may be cached and is not guaranteed to be up-to-date in real-time unless the value was returned by `/accounts/balance/get`. If `current` is `null` this field is guaranteed not to be `null`.
---@field current number|distilled.Null The total amount of funds in or owed by the account. For `credit`-type accounts, a positive balance indicates the amount owed; a negative amount indicates the lender owing the account holder. For `loan`-type accounts, the current balance is the principal remaining on the loan, except in the case of student loan accounts at Sallie Mae (`ins_116944`). For Sallie Mae student loans, the account's balance includes both principal and any outstanding interest. For `investment`-type accounts (or `brokerage`-type accounts for API versions 2018-05-22 and earlier), the current balance is the total value of assets as presented by the institution. Note that balance information may be cached unless the value was returned by `/accounts/balance/get`; if the Item is enabled for Transactions, the balance will be at least as recent as the most recent Transaction update. If you require real-time balance information, use the `available` balance as provided by `/accounts/balance/get`. When returned by `/accounts/balance/get`, this field may be `null`. When this happens, `available` is guaranteed not to be `null`.
---@field limit number|distilled.Null For `credit`-type accounts, this represents the credit limit. For `depository`-type accounts, this represents the pre-arranged overdraft limit, which is common for current (checking) accounts in Europe. In North America, this field is typically only available for `credit`-type accounts.
---@field iso_currency_code string|distilled.Null The ISO-4217 currency code of the balance. Always null if `unofficial_currency_code` is non-null.
---@field unofficial_currency_code string|distilled.Null The unofficial currency code associated with the balance. Always null if `iso_currency_code` is non-null. Unofficial currency codes are used for currencies that do not have official ISO currency codes, such as cryptocurrencies and the currencies of certain countries. See the [currency code schema](https://plaid.com/docs/api/accounts#currency-code-schema) for a full listing of supported `unofficial_currency_code`s.
---@field last_updated_datetime? string|distilled.Null Timestamp in [ISO 8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ`) indicating the oldest acceptable balance when making a request to `/accounts/balance/get`. This field is only used and expected when the institution is `ins_128026` (Capital One) and the Item contains one or more accounts with a non-depository account type, in which case a value must be provided or an `INVALID_REQUEST` error with the code of `INVALID_FIELD` will be returned. For Capital One depository accounts as well as all other account types on all other institutions, this field is ignored. See [account type schema](https://plaid.com/docs/api/accounts/#account-type-schema) for a full list of account types. If the balance that is pulled is older than the given timestamp for Items with this field required, an `INVALID_RESULT` error with the code of `LAST_UPDATED_DATETIME_OUT_OF_RANGE` will be returned with the most recent timestamp for the requested account contained in the response.
---@field average_balance? number|distilled.Null The average historical balance for the entire report
---@field average_monthly_balances? plaid.BaseReportAccountBalancesAverageMonthlyBalancesList The average historical balance of each calendar month
---@field most_recent_thirty_day_average_balance? number|distilled.Null The average historical balance from the most recent 30 days

---The average historical balance of each calendar month
---@alias plaid.BaseReportAccountBalancesAverageMonthlyBalancesList plaid.BaseReportAverageMonthlyBalances[]

---The information about previously submitted valid dispute statements by the consumer
---@alias plaid.BaseReportAccountConsumerDisputesList plaid.ConsumerDispute[]

