---Details about the fraud analysis performed on the document.
---@class plaid.FraudAnalysisDetails
---@field type_supported plaid.FraudCheckOutcome Whether the submitted document type is supported for fraud analysis. `success` - The document type is supported. `failed` - The document type is not supported.
---@field portrait_presence_check plaid.FraudCheckOutcome The outcome of the portrait presence check. `success` - A portrait was detected. `failed` - No portrait was detected.
---@field portrait_details_check plaid.FraudCheckOutcome The outcome of the portrait details check including photo embedding and face landmark checks. `success` - The portrait passed all validity checks. `failed` - The portrait did not pass one or more validity checks.
---@field image_composition_check plaid.FraudCheckOutcome The outcome of the image composition check. `success` - The image is a valid physical document capture. `failed` - The image appears to be a photograph of a screen or a digital forgery.
---@field integrity_check plaid.FraudCheckOutcome The outcome of the integrity check for document security elements. `success` - Data is consistent across all checked security elements. `failed` - Inconsistencies were detected across one or more security elements.
---@field detail_check plaid.FraudCheckOutcome The outcome of the document detail check for correct styling and layout. `success` - The document passed all authenticity checks. `failed` - The document did not pass one or more authenticity checks.
---@field issue_date_check plaid.FraudCheckOutcomeWithNoData The outcome of the issue date validity check. `success` - The issue date is valid. `failed` - The issue date is invalid or could not be verified. `no_data` - The check could not be performed due to insufficient data.
---@field [string] any

---Event fraud attributes as an arbitrary set of key-value pairs. The set of attributes returned varies by model.
---@alias plaid.FraudAttributes { [string]: any }

---The outcome of the fraud check.
---
---
---`success` - The check passed.
---
---`failed` - The check did not pass.
---@alias plaid.FraudCheckOutcome "success"|"failed"

---The outcome of the fraud check.
---
---
---`success` - The check passed.
---
---`failed` - The check did not pass.
---
---`no_data` - The check could not be performed due to insufficient data.
---@alias plaid.FraudCheckOutcomeWithNoData "success"|"failed"|"no_data"

