---Insights into gambling-related transactions, including frequency, amounts, and top merchants.
---@class plaid.GamblingIndicators
---@field amount? number|distilled.Null The total value of transactions that fall into the `GAMBLING` credit category, across all the accounts in the report.
---@field iso_currency_code? string|distilled.Null The ISO-4217 currency code of the amount. Always `null` if `unofficial_currency_code` is non-`null`.
---@field unofficial_currency_code? string|distilled.Null The unofficial currency code associated with the amount. Always `null` if `iso_currency_code` is non-`null`. See the [currency code schema](https://plaid.com/docs/api/accounts#currency-code-schema) for a full listing of supported `unofficial_currency_code`s.
---@field monthly_average? plaid.MonthlyAverage|distilled.Null
---@field top_merchants? plaid.GamblingIndicatorsTopMerchantsList Up to 3 top merchants that the user had the most transactions for in the given time window, in descending order of total spend. If the user has not spent money on any merchants in the given time window, this list will be empty.
---@field transactions_count? number|distilled.Null The total number of transactions that fall into the `GAMBLING` credit category, across all the accounts in the report.
---@field monthly_summaries? plaid.GamblingIndicatorsMonthlySummariesList The monthly summaries of the transactions that fall into the `GAMBLING` category within the given time window, across all the accounts in the report.
---@field days_since_last_occurrence? number|distilled.Null The number of days since the last transaction that falls into the `GAMBLING` category, across all the accounts in the report.
---@field percentage_of_income? number|distilled.Null The percentage of the user's monthly inflows that was spent on transactions that fall into the `GAMBLING` category within the given time window, across all the accounts in the report. For example, a value of 100 indicates that 100% of the inflows were spent on transactions that fall into the `GAMBLING` credit category. If there's no available income for the given time period, this field value will be `-1`
---@field [string] any

---The monthly summaries of the transactions that fall into the `GAMBLING` category within the given time window, across all the accounts in the report.
