---A transaction within an investment account.
---@class plaid.InvestmentTransaction
---@field investment_transaction_id string The ID of the Investment transaction, unique across all Plaid transactions. Like all Plaid identifiers, the `investment_transaction_id` is case sensitive.
---@field cancel_transaction_id? string|distilled.Null A legacy field formerly used internally by Plaid to identify certain canceled transactions.
---@field account_id string The `account_id` of the account against which this transaction posted.
---@field security_id string|distilled.Null The `security_id` to which this transaction is related.
---@field date string The [ISO 8601](https://wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) posting date for the transaction. This is typically the settlement date.
---@field transaction_datetime? string|distilled.Null Timestamp in [ISO 8601](https://wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ`) representing when the order was initiated. This field is returned for select financial institutions and reflects the value provided by the institution. When the institution only provides a date without time-of-day information, this field will reflect the date that the order was initiated with a time component that defaults to `T00:00:00Z`. This does not indicate that the order was initiated at midnight UTC.
---@field name string The institution's description of the transaction.
---@field quantity number The number of units of the security involved in this transaction. Positive for buy transactions; negative for sell transactions.
---@field amount number The complete value of the transaction. Positive values when cash is debited, e.g. purchases of stock; negative values when cash is credited, e.g. sales of stock. Treatment remains the same for cash-only movements unassociated with securities. For transactions representing a simultaneous cash contribution and purchase of a security, the portion of the transaction representing the purchase takes precedence, and the `amount` is represented as positive.
---@field price number The price of the security at which this transaction occurred.
---@field fees number|distilled.Null The combined value of all fees applied to this transaction
---@field type plaid.InvestmentTransactionType
---@field subtype plaid.InvestmentTransactionSubtype
---@field iso_currency_code string|distilled.Null The ISO-4217 currency code of the transaction. Always `null` if `unofficial_currency_code` is non-`null`.
---@field unofficial_currency_code string|distilled.Null The unofficial currency code associated with the transaction. Always `null` if `iso_currency_code` is non-`null`. Unofficial currency codes are used for currencies that do not have official ISO currency codes, such as cryptocurrencies and the currencies of certain countries. See the [currency code schema](https://plaid.com/docs/api/accounts#currency-code-schema) for a full listing of supported `unofficial_currency_code`s.
---@field [string] any

---For descriptions of possible transaction types and subtypes, see the [Investment transaction types schema](https://plaid.com/docs/api/accounts/#investment-transaction-types-schema).
---@alias plaid.InvestmentTransactionSubtype "account fee"|"adjustment"|"assignment"|"buy"|"buy to cover"|"contribution"|"deposit"|"distribution"|"dividend"|"dividend reinvestment"|"exercise"|"expire"|"interest"|"interest receivable"|"interest reinvestment"|"legal fee"|"long-term capital gain"|"long-term capital gain reinvestment"|"management fee"|"margin expense"|"merger"|"miscellaneous fee"|"non-qualified dividend"|"non-resident tax"|"pending credit"|"pending debit"|"qualified dividend"|"return of principal"|"request"|"sell"|"sell short"|"send"|"short-term capital gain"|"short-term capital gain reinvestment"|"spin off"|"split"|"stock distribution"|"tax"|"tax withheld"|"trade"|"transfer"|"transfer fee"|"trust fee"|"unqualified gain"|"withdrawal"

---Value is one of the following:
---
---`buy`: Buying an investment
---
---`sell`: Selling an investment
---
---`cancel`: A cancellation of a pending transaction
---
---`cash`: Activity that modifies a cash position
---
---`fee`: A fee on the account
---
---`transfer`: Activity which modifies a position, but not through buy/sell activity e.g. options exercise, portfolio transfer
---
---For descriptions of possible transaction types and subtypes, see the [Investment transaction types schema](https://plaid.com/docs/api/accounts/#investment-transaction-types-schema).
---@alias plaid.InvestmentTransactionType "buy"|"sell"|"cancel"|"cash"|"fee"|"transfer"

