---Metadata about the Item
---@class plaid.ItemWithConsentFields
---@field item_id string The Plaid Item ID. The `item_id` is always unique; linking the same account at the same institution twice will result in two Items with different `item_id` values. Like all Plaid identifiers, the `item_id` is case-sensitive.
---@field institution_id? string|distilled.Null The Plaid Institution ID associated with the Item. Field is omitted for Items created without an institution connection, such as Items created via Same-Day Micro-deposits.
---@field institution_name? string|distilled.Null The name of the institution associated with the Item. Field is omitted for Items created without an institution connection, such as Items created via Same-Day Micro-deposits.
---@field webhook string|distilled.Null The URL registered to receive webhooks for the Item. Empty string if no webhook is set.
---@field auth_method? plaid.ItemAuthMethod|distilled.Null
---@field error plaid.PlaidError|distilled.Null
---@field available_products plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsAvailableProductsList A list of products available for the Item that have not yet been accessed. The contents of this array will be mutually exclusive with `billed_products`.
---@field billed_products plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsBilledProductsList A list of products that have been billed for the Item. The contents of this array will be mutually exclusive with `available_products`. Note - `billed_products` is populated in all environments but only requests in Production are billed. Also note that products that are billed on a pay-per-call basis rather than a pay-per-Item basis, such as `balance`, will not appear here.
---@field products? plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsProductsList A list of products added to the Item. In almost all cases, this will be the same as the `billed_products` field. For some products, it is possible for the product to be added to an Item but not yet billed (e.g. Assets, before `/asset_report/create` has been called, or Auth or Identity when added as Optional Products but before their endpoints have been called), in which case the product may appear in `products` but not in `billed_products`.
---@field consented_products? plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsConsentedProductsList A list of products that the user has consented to for the Item via [Data Transparency Messaging](https://plaid.com/docs/link/data-transparency-messaging-migration-guide). This will consist of all products where both of the following are true: the user has consented to the required data scopes for that product and you have Production access for that product.
---@field consent_expiration_time string|distilled.Null The date and time at which the Item's access consent will expire, in [ISO 8601](https://wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format. If the Item does not have consent expiration scheduled, this field will be `null`. Currently, only institutions in Europe and a small number of institutions in the US have expiring consent. For a list of US institutions that currently expire consent, see the [OAuth Guide](https://plaid.com/docs/link/oauth/#refreshing-item-consent).
---@field update_type plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsUpdateType Indicates whether an Item requires user interaction to be updated, which can be the case for Items with some forms of two-factor authentication. `background` - Item can be updated in the background `user_present_required` - Item requires user interaction to be updated
---@field paired_item_id? string|distilled.Null The `item_id` of the Item that was created alongside this one when a single Link session used both Plaid Inc and Plaid Check products (see [Using Plaid Check products alongside Plaid products](https://plaid.com/docs/check/add-to-app/#using-plaid-check-products-alongside-plaid-products)). For a Plaid Inc Item, this is the paired Plaid Check Item, and the reverse for a Plaid Check Item. The field is omitted for Items that have no paired Item. It is also omitted if Plaid cannot look up the paired Item at request time, so do not treat its absence as proof that an Item is unpaired.
---@field created_at? string The date and time when the Item was created, in [ISO 8601](https://wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format.
---@field consented_use_cases? plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsConsentedUseCasesList A list of use cases that the user has consented to for the Item via [Data Transparency Messaging](https://plaid.com/docs/link/data-transparency-messaging-migration-guide). You can see the full list of use cases or update the list of use cases to request at any time via the Link Customization section of the [Plaid Dashboard](https://dashboard.plaid.com/link/data-transparency-v5).
---@field consented_data_scopes? plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsConsentedDataScopesList A list of data scopes that the user has consented to for the Item via [Data Transparency Messaging](https://plaid.com/docs/link/data-transparency-messaging-migration-guide). These are based on the `consented_products`; see the [full mapping](https://plaid.com/docs/link/data-transparency-messaging-migration-guide/#data-scopes-by-product) of data scopes and products.
---@field [string] any

---A list of products available for the Item that have not yet been accessed. The contents of this array will be mutually exclusive with `billed_products`.
---@alias plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsAvailableProductsList plaid.Products[]

---A list of products that have been billed for the Item. The contents of this array will be mutually exclusive with `available_products`. Note - `billed_products` is populated in all environments but only requests in Production are billed. Also note that products that are billed on a pay-per-call basis rather than a pay-per-Item basis, such as `balance`, will not appear here.
---@alias plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsBilledProductsList plaid.Products[]

---A list of data scopes that the user has consented to for the Item via [Data Transparency Messaging](https://plaid.com/docs/link/data-transparency-messaging-migration-guide). These are based on the `consented_products`; see the [full mapping](https://plaid.com/docs/link/data-transparency-messaging-migration-guide/#data-scopes-by-product) of data scopes and products.
---@alias plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsConsentedDataScopesList plaid.ItemConsentedDataScope[]

---A list of products that the user has consented to for the Item via [Data Transparency Messaging](https://plaid.com/docs/link/data-transparency-messaging-migration-guide). This will consist of all products where both of the following are true: the user has consented to the required data scopes for that product and you have Production access for that product.
---@alias plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsConsentedProductsList plaid.Products[]

---A list of use cases that the user has consented to for the Item via [Data Transparency Messaging](https://plaid.com/docs/link/data-transparency-messaging-migration-guide).
---
---You can see the full list of use cases or update the list of use cases to request at any time via the Link Customization section of the [Plaid Dashboard](https://dashboard.plaid.com/link/data-transparency-v5).
---@alias plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsConsentedUseCasesList string[]

---A list of products added to the Item. In almost all cases, this will be the same as the `billed_products` field. For some products, it is possible for the product to be added to an Item but not yet billed (e.g. Assets, before `/asset_report/create` has been called, or Auth or Identity when added as Optional Products but before their endpoints have been called), in which case the product may appear in `products` but not in `billed_products`.
---@alias plaid.ItemWithConsentFieldsProductsList plaid.Products[]

---Indicates whether an Item requires user interaction to be updated, which can be the case for Items with some forms of two-factor authentication.
