---A JSON Web Key (JWK) that can be used in conjunction with [JWT libraries](https://jwt.io/#libraries-io) to verify Plaid webhooks
---@class plaid.JWKPublicKey
---@field alg string The alg member identifies the cryptographic algorithm family used with the key.
---@field crv string The crv member identifies the cryptographic curve used with the key.
---@field kid string The kid (Key ID) member can be used to match a specific key. This can be used, for instance, to choose among a set of keys within the JWK during key rollover.
---@field kty string The kty (key type) parameter identifies the cryptographic algorithm family used with the key, such as RSA or EC.
---@field use string The use (public key use) parameter identifies the intended use of the public key.
---@field x string The x member contains the x coordinate for the elliptic curve point, provided as a base64url-encoded string of the coordinate's big endian representation.
---@field y string The y member contains the y coordinate for the elliptic curve point, provided as a base64url-encoded string of the coordinate's big endian representation.
---@field created_at number The timestamp when the key was created, in Unix time.
---@field expired_at number|distilled.Null The timestamp when the key expired, in Unix time.
---@field [string] any

